WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.560
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar reminding you to mind your decisions.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:10.820
A square has a triangle inside of it with lengths of 4, 3, and 5.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.520
What is the value of x, the length of the square's side?

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.960
I've adapted this problem from one I saw online.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.180
Pause the video if you'd like to give it a try,

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:27.440
and when you're ready, keep watching to learn how to solve this problem.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.140
So, how can we solve for x, the length of the square's side?

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:52.740
First, notice that the triangle has lengths of 3, 4, and 5, and that means it's a right triangle.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:59.420
The angle between the sides of 3 and 4 will be a right angle and measures 90 degrees.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.940
Now let's focus on these two triangles.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:08.700
We're going to show that this triangle (lower left) is similar to this triangle (upper left).

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:15.100
How can we do that? We're going to show that they have exactly the same angles.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:20.280
To get started, let's label this angle as 'a.'

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.560
Here we have a right angle because we have a square,

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:29.040
therefore, the other angle in this square will be (90-a)°.

00:01:30.179 --> 00:01:32.749
Now, let's calculate this angle here.

00:01:33.959 --> 00:01:35.549
We need it to be

00:01:35.549 --> 00:01:39.469
180° minus the other two angles along this straight line.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:46.800
So this angle will be 180°- [right angle] - [other angle].

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:49.260
Which equals 90°- a.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.640
When we simplify this we just get a°.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:58.040
Now, we have a right angle here in this corner of the square,

00:01:58.409 --> 00:02:02.478
so the final angle in this triangle will be (90°- a°).

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:09.229
We can see corresponding angles of these two triangles are equal, and therefore these two triangles are similar.
(by the AAA Theorem)

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.420
But how does that help us solve the problem?

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:16.620
Well, let's label the shorter side of this triangle as 'y.'

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:23.140
Since the entire side of the square is equal to x, this distance will be (x - y).

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:27.500
Now we use the property that these two triangles are similar

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:32.500
therefore the ratio of their long leg to their hypotenuse will be equal so

00:02:33.359 --> 00:02:37.579
(x - y) / 3 = x / 4

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.760
We'll solve this equation for y.

00:02:41.579 --> 00:02:43.579
Cross multiply.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.100
Distribute.

00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:48.319
Simplify.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:54.280
We get x = 4y which means y = x/4

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.900
We'll substitute that into our diagram here.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:04.620
We can now solve for x because we have a right triangle and we're going to use the distance formula.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:09.730
x^2 + (x/4)^2 = 4^2

00:03:10.909 --> 00:03:15.489
17x²/16 = 16

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:22.779
For x &gt; 0 we have a value that x = 16/√(17)

00:03:23.389 --> 00:03:25.389
That's the answer.

00:03:25.639 --> 00:03:29.259
It's a fun little geometry problem, and I hope you enjoyed it, too.

00:03:30.349 --> 00:03:34.089
Thanks for making Mind Your Decisions one of the best channels on YouTube.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:38.080
Thanks for watching and thanks for your support.

